Data model
  Category (cr1a2_category): name
  Subcategory (cr1a2_subcategory): name, cr1a2_category (lookup to Category)
  Request (cr1a2_request): cr1a2_category (lookup), cr1a2_subcategory (lookup)

No-code route (try first)
  In the Dataverse form designer: select the Subcategory lookup > Properties > Filtering >
    Filter by related rows: Category (Requests) > Category (Subcategories)
  Basic form metadata (Portal Management > Basic Form Metadata), for both lookups:
    Control Style: Render Lookup as Dropdown
  Power Pages honours related-records filtering for lookups rendered as drop-downs on many form
  configurations. If the child does not refresh on change in your site version, use the script route.

Script route
  Site settings:  Webapi/cr1a2_subcategory/enabled = true      Webapi/cr1a2_subcategory/fields = cr1a2_name,cr1a2_subcategoryid,_cr1a2_category_value
  Table permission: Subcategory, Global, Read, for the role using the form (Category likewise).
  Both lookups rendered as drop-downs. Requires the safeAjax wrapper (see the Web API patterns).

$(document).ready(function () {
  var $parent = $("#cr1a2_category");
  var $child = $("#cr1a2_subcategory");
  var initialChild = $child.val();

  function setOptions(rows, keep) {
    $child.empty().append($("<option>").val("").text("Select"));
    rows.forEach(function (r) {
      $child.append($("<option>").val(r.cr1a2_subcategoryid).text(r.cr1a2_name));
    });
    if (keep && $child.find("option[value='" + keep + "']").length) { $child.val(keep); }
    $child.prop("disabled", rows.length === 0).trigger("change");
  }

  function load(keep) {
    var parentId = $parent.val();
    if (!parentId) { setOptions([], null); return; }
    webapi.safeAjax({
      type: "GET",
      url: "/_api/cr1a2_subcategories?$select=cr1a2_name,cr1a2_subcategoryid" +
           "&$filter=_cr1a2_category_value eq " + parentId + " and statecode eq 0&$orderby=cr1a2_name",
      contentType: "application/json"
    }).done(function (res) { setOptions(res.value, keep); })
      .fail(function () { setOptions([], null); });
  }

  $parent.on("change", function () { load(null); });
  load(initialChild);          // edit forms: keep the saved value
});

Why this works with the form's save
  A lookup rendered as a drop-down posts the selected option's value (the GUID) with hidden fields for the
  name and table. Replacing options keeps the same select element, so the form saves normally.
  If your form version uses hidden inputs #cr1a2_subcategory_name and #cr1a2_subcategory_entityname,
  update them on change:
    $child.on("change", function () {
      $("#cr1a2_subcategory_name").val($child.find("option:selected").text());
      $("#cr1a2_subcategory_entityname").val("cr1a2_subcategory");
    });

Choice columns instead of lookups
  Two choice columns cannot be related in Dataverse. Hide the options that do not apply:
    var map = { "100000000": ["100000000","100000001"], "100000001": ["100000002","100000003"] };
    var $all = $("#cr1a2_subtype option").clone();
    $("#cr1a2_type").on("change", function () {
      var allowed = map[$(this).val()] || [];
      $("#cr1a2_subtype").empty().append($all.filter(function () { return this.value === "" || allowed.indexOf(this.value) > -1; }).clone());
    }).trigger("change");
  The mapping lives in script, so lookups are easier to maintain.

Without the Web API (Liquid-rendered data)
